{"id":"n-20261011-h96l1v","category":"travel","display_title":"Historic European Spa Towns","display_title_he":"עיירות מרפא היסטוריות באירופה","short_summary":"Explore historic European spa towns designated by Unesco, known for centuries-old healing traditions, thermal waters, and stunning architecture.","english_level":"C1","words":463,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Beauregard_Town_Historic_District%2C_Baton_Rouge%2C_LA%2C_US.jpg/960px-Beauregard_Town_Historic_District%2C_Baton_Rouge%2C_LA%2C_US.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Bubba73 · CC BY-SA 3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beauregard_Town_Historic_District,_Baton_Rouge,_LA,_US.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/travel/2026/oct/11/best-spa-towns-europe-autumn-wellbeing-holiday","title":"Healing waters: 10 of the best spa towns in Europe for a restorative autumn break","published_at":"2026-10-11T06:00:18.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-11T06:00:18.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-11T15:08:03.077Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Europe boasts a rich heritage of wellness tourism that reached its zenith between 1700 and the 1930s. In 2021, Unesco recognized this cultural phenomenon by designating eleven historic spa towns across the continent as a single transnational world heritage site. These grand destinations, ranging from alpine valleys to belle époque resorts, invite travelers to experience centuries-old healing treatments, steaming mineral pools, and therapeutic treatments in stunning historical settings.","Among the most remarkable locations is Mariánské Lázně in Czechia, celebrated for its picturesque architecture and three distinct natural healing traditions: mineral springs, carbon dioxide springs called Maria’s Gas, and therapeutic peloids consisting of mud and clay. Visitors can still stay at the canary yellow neo-renaissance Nové Lázně hotel, where King Edward VII once stayed and took the waters, and enjoy traditional sweet hazelnut or chocolate-filled spa wafers alongside locals drinking from porcelain cups along the elegant colonnades.","Germany hosts about 350 designated spa towns, including Bad Kissingen in Bavaria. Here, star architect Max Littmann shaped much of the central district in the early 20th century, creating magnificent structures such as the grand fountain hall with its stained-glass roof and the art nouveau Regentenbau concert hall, which houses one of the best concert halls in Europe. Meanwhile, deeper north in the Black Forest, Bad Wildbad combines thermal soaking with outdoor adventures. Visitors can ride a funicular up to Sommerberg, walk along an elevated Treetop Walk, or cross a massive Wildline suspension bridge before relaxing in historic thermal baths surrounded by marble pillars and Moorish tiles.","Further west in Normandy, Bagnoles de l'Orne offers a distinct charm born from a medieval legend about a nobleman, Seigneur Hugues de Tessé, and his miraculous warhorse Rapide. The local belle époque quartier features gorgeous villas near a lake in the Andaines forest, where guests can enjoy cycling, mushroom foraging among over 1,700 varieties, and restorative treatments in partnership with a nearby resort. In the Austrian Alps, Bad Gastein offers a dramatic mountain backdrop with radon-rich thermal waters that once attracted historical figures like Sigmund Freud, alongside brutalist bath complexes and cozy alpine cabins serving kaspressknödelsuppe.","In Slovakia, the island town of Piešťany welcomes visitors with a symbolic statue of a man breaking his crutch, reflecting the potency of its thermal waters and sulphurous mud. Guests at the stately Thermia Palace can experience traditional mud packs before exploring the vibrant local cultural scene. Finally, eastern Slovenia features Rogaška, a town renowned for Donat Mg, an exceptionally magnesium-rich mineral water that visitors can sample directly from the fountains.","Across all these historic destinations, the tradition of taking the waters continues to thrive. Whether visitors seek relief from chronic ailments, architectural wonder, or simply a restorative autumn break, Europe's grand spa towns offer a timeless journey into wellness and relaxation."],"facts":[{"fact":"In 2021, Unesco designated 11 historic spa towns across Europe as a transnational world heritage site.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Mariánské Lázně in Czechia offers three natural healing traditions: mineral springs, carbon dioxide springs known as Maria’s Gas, and therapeutic peloids.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Bad Kissingen in Bavaria features stunning architecture rebuilt by Max Littmann in the early 20th century.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Bad Wildbad in the Black Forest offers thermal springs alongside nature activities like a Treetop Walk and a suspension bridge.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Bagnoles de l'Orne in Normandy developed around warm, sulphurous waters connected to a medieval legend about a warhorse.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Bad Gastein in the Austrian Alps features radon-rich thermal springs and historic appeal once visited by Sigmund Freud.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Piešťany in Slovakia utilizes sulphurous mud and thermal waters on its Spa Island, symbolized by a statue of a man breaking his crutch.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Rogaška in eastern Slovenia is famous for Donat Mg, an extremely magnesium-rich mineral water.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Europe","lemma":"Europe","pos":"noun","he":"אירופה","name":"true"},{"text":"boasts","lemma":"boast","pos":"verb","he":"מתגאה","name":false},{"text":"rich","lemma":"rich","pos":"adjective","he":"עשיר","name":false},{"text":"heritage","lemma":"heritage","pos":"noun","he":"מורשת","name":false},{"text":"wellness","lemma":"wellness","pos":"noun","he":"בריאות / רווחה","name":false},{"text":"tourism","lemma":"tourism","pos":"noun","he":"תיירות","name":false},{"text":"reached","lemma":"reach","pos":"verb","he":"הגיע","name":false},{"text":"zenith","lemma":"zenith","pos":"noun","he":"שיא","name":false},{"text":"between","lemma":"between","pos":"preposition","he":"בין","name":false},{"text":"Unesco","lemma":"Unesco","pos":"noun","he":"אונסק\"ו","name":"true"},{"text":"recognized","lemma":"recognize","pos":"verb","he":"הכיר ב־","name":false},{"text":"cultural","lemma":"cultural","pos":"adjective","he":"תרבותי","name":false},{"text":"phenomenon","lemma":"phenomenon","pos":"noun","he":"תופעה","name":false},{"text":"designating","lemma":"designate","pos":"verb","he":"ציון / הגדרה","name":false},{"text":"historic","lemma":"historic","pos":"adjective","he":"היסטורי","name":false},{"text":"spa towns","lemma":"spa town","pos":"noun","he":"עיירות מרפא","name":false},{"text":"continent","lemma":"continent","pos":"noun","he":"יבשת","name":false},{"text":"transnational","lemma":"transnational","pos":"adjective","he":"בין-לאומי","name":false},{"text":"world heritage site","lemma":"world heritage site","pos":"noun","he":"אתר מורשת עולמית","name":false},{"text":"destinations","lemma":"destination","pos":"noun","he":"יעדים","name":false},{"text":"alpine","lemma":"alpine","pos":"adjective","he":"אלפיני","name":false},{"text":"valleys","lemma":"valley","pos":"noun","he":"עמקים","name":false},{"text":"belle époque","lemma":"belle époque","pos":"adjective","he":"התקופה היפה (בלה אפוק)","name":false},{"text":"resorts","lemma":"resort","pos":"noun","he":"אתרי נופש","name":false},{"text":"travelers","lemma":"traveler","pos":"noun","he":"מטיילים","name":false},{"text":"experience","lemma":"experience","pos":"verb","he":"לחוות","name":false},{"text":"centuries-old","lemma":"centuries-old","pos":"adjective","he":"בן מאות שנים","name":false},{"text":"healing","lemma":"healing","pos":"adjective","he":"מרפא","name":false},{"text":"